Self value (scalar)
description: the self-value's types - JSON Schema's set, binary added, its own subtyping

- >
  Each omnivorous node can have a self value (or scalar).

- 'A whole yamlover document may be nothing but one scalar - a leaf. A string:'
- !!yo Grey tabby, adopted 2019
- 'A number, a boolean, a null:'
- !!yo 30
- !!yo true
- !!yo ~
- 'Quotes force a string - this document holds text, not a number:'
- !!yo '30'
- 'And a block scalar carries multi-line text - still one value:'
- !!yo |
  A multi-line self value —
  one string, kept verbatim.

- > The value belongs to one of these types

- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Yamlover name
    - JSON Schema name
    - Type description
      width: 2
    - Examples
  - - str
    - string
    - 'Unicode text. Quoting forces it - `''1''` is the string, bare `1` is not. Refined by `format`; a bare string''s default prose format is `text/marklower`.'
    - '`Hello, *world*` · `''42''`'
  - - int
    - integer
    - 'A whole number - the subtype of `float` whose value has no fractional part.'
    - '`30` · `-7` · `0`'
  - - float
    - number
    - 'Any number, whole or fractional. JSON Schema calls the same type `number`; `int` is its subtype.'
    - '`3.14` · `-2.5` · `6.02e23`'
  - - bool
    - boolean
    - 'The two truth values - nothing else coerces to them.'
    - '`true` · `false`'
  - - 'null'
    - 'null'
    - 'The singleton - its only value is `null`, so the type is also a value. A bare key `a:` means `a: null`.'
    - '`~` · `null` · a bare `a:`'
  - - binary
    - '- (none)'
    - 'Opaque bytes - the yamlover addition; JSON Schema has no bytes type. Refined by `format` (`image/png`, `int32/le`); usually stored as a file, and YAML''s `!!binary` (base64) is the same value.'
    - 'the bytes of `logo.png` · `!!binary R0lGODlh...`'
- >
  A scalar may carry a **format** - JSON Schema's own (`date-time`, `email`, `uri`) and, beyond
  them, `text/markdown`, `image/png`, `int32/le` - a named constraint refining how the value is
  decoded, rendered, and edited; a bare string's default prose format is `text/marklower`. The
  [format chapter](::language:model:format) is its subject.


